# Project guidance for cursor

<!-- Generated from platform-configs/shared by scripts/project-guidance.py. -->

Use for projects that consume .cursorrules. Respect scoped rules in the project.

## Project context

Use the current project's purpose, audience and approved data sources. Load one relevant profile. Keep personal, employer and client records in their own authorized workspace. Ask for missing context only when it changes the work.

## Work and verification

Follow the project's instructions, naming conventions and existing tests. Choose one workflow owner. Use project-router for lifecycle decisions when available, and use a specialist directly for a bounded task. Check the result against the request and report which checks actually ran.

For dated plans and reports use `YYYYMMDD - {Tool/Project} - {Short Concise Description}` and the project owner's local date. Match a Markdown report's H1 to its filename stem. Machine entrypoints keep the filenames their tools require.

## Tools and access

Read the project's settings and dependencies to identify its stack. Work within the tools and permissions available in the receiving host. Use public or synthetic examples for shared material. Confirm the destination and existing authorization before publishing, installing software, changing production or sending data to another service.
